```
$ jci-coverage report --help
Writes `coverage/lcov.info` and prints a terminal summary. Requires
`cargo-llvm-cov` and the `llvm-tools` rustup component on PATH (and
`cargo-nextest` too, when `--runner nextest` is selected).

Usage: jci-coverage report [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --package <NAME>
          Limit coverage to one workspace package

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase logging verbosity

  -q, --quiet...
          Decrease logging verbosity

      --runner <RUNNER>
          Test runner to drive coverage with

          Possible values:
          - test:    `cargo llvm-cov` — plain `cargo test`
          - nextest: `cargo llvm-cov nextest` — needs `cargo-nextest`
            too
          
          [default: test]

      --nextest-profile <NAME>
          Nextest profile to use.
          
          Only meaningful with `--runner nextest`.

      --no-all-features
          Disable `--all-features` (on by default).
          
          Matches `toolkit/code_coverage`, so instrumented subprocess
          coverage is captured.

      --dry-run
          Preview the cargo-llvm-cov invocation without running it.
          
          Never fails on a missing tool or touches the filesystem —
          works with zero tool setup, so it's usable for previewing
          the exact argv, and for anything (CI smoke checks, this
          crate's own CLI tests) that wants to exercise this command's
          logging without cargo-llvm-cov installed at all. Still warns
          (without failing) when a required tool is missing, so the
          preview stays honest about whether a real run would actually
          work.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

```
